 {:seon.task/name "a-request-is-finished-from-its-page-in-about-twenty-turns" :seon.task/plan "The free context audit's gate before any paid run (owner: \"Only use paid runs though when we legitimately have solved the known problems with our context ... fix the problems ... at the root\"). The known problems P1-P9: the archived paper known-context-problems-2026-10-26.md (git history); audit 1: the archived paper context-audit-1-2026-10-26.md (git history); audit 2 (main 735daa366): the archived paper context-audit-2-2026-10-27.md (git history), NOT CLEAN: yes help, bytes; likely related-list, message, first-sentence, cut-char, star; at risk mixed, namespaced; no long-string. Audit 3's prerequisites, each on main first: agent view: a cited var's source and its tests drawn as separate children under their own budgets (`seon.render.ui/cited`; the source starved print-value's 27 tests), the related part drawn through related-view's lines not bare addresses (`seon.render.ui/related`), the plan's duplicate in a title attribute and the empty parts gone; ctx-atom: a cited var's tests listed by reach, not only direct callers (my.agent/tests-reaching, on jolt/a-cited-vars-tests-are-its-own-query), and the call graph followed from the cited entry to the fix site (trim-word, first-sentence, member-rank and allot went uncited); the incremental index's correctness red (r3.inc-test/incremental-equals-full) fixed; then the instructions' existing-tests pointer swapped from my.agent/callers to my.agent/tests-reaching within the 1,200-char bound (`seon.template/instructions`). Audit 3 runs as audits 1 and 2 did: a fresh worktree of main, the ten requests (`seon.fixtures/requests`) written through `seon.template/request` on its root with no model, each reproduction evaluated on main first (a request that answers right is replaced), each first-turn context read through the server's :context op, and a fresh Sonnet reviewer judging each against its request and P1-P9 with one verdict. Only